  {
    "@id": "https://www.centrekabir.com/temporary/9c484e0a-063a-4986-81e8-e96d1ead7066",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.centrekabir.com/en/events/nexgen-festival-gold/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Since 2021, we have been celebrating Canadian authors of South Asian origin writing in diverse genres at GOLD - the Garden of Literary Delights, a unique literary event in Montreal."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSince 2021, we have been celebrating Canadian authors of South Asian origin writing in diverse genres at GOLD – the Garden of Literary Delights, a unique literary event in Montreal. It is part of the NexGen MultiArts Festival of the Kabir Cultural Centre.We have a stellar line-up for 2025 too:Torontonian, Deepa Rajagopalan, presenting her powerful short story collection, Peacocks of Instagram, shortlisted for the 2024 Giller prize.Torontonian Aamir Hussain, reading from Under the Full and Cresent Moon (Fall 2025), a wonderful debut novel about an Islamic matriarchy in the past.Giller-prize long-listed author Arjun Basu, a Montrealer, reading from his acclaimed “family” novel, The Reeds (2024). He is also creative on several platforms.Aditya Banerjee, award-winning, best-selling author of mystery novels reading from Secret of the Missing Tenant (2025), set in Delhi, Bombay and Rajasthan. Banerjee is also a Montrealer.Plus Indian munchies, conversation, community, book sale and book signing, giveaways…\nAdmission Free, donations appreciated!\nPlease RSVP at info@centrekabir.com\n"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g4133200"
      }
    ],
